<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neungsan-ri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Neungsan-ri tombs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neungsan-ri is a site in Buyeo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, with a group of royal tombs of the Sabi period of Baekje (538–660) and the remains of a temple next to them. In 1993 excavators of the temple site found the Gilt-bronze <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">Incense</a> Burner of Baekje, a masterpiece of East Asian metalwork. The tombs and temple are part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baekje-historic-areas">Baekje Historic Areas</a> World Heritage Site.</p></div>
